  "summary": "The code contains a critical security vulnerability due to disabled SSL verification and significant performance bottlenecks from synchronous I/O. Overall health is poor due to lack of input validation, type safety, and hardcoded configurations. The refactored code introduces a persistent session, input validation, and proper documentation.",
  "fixed_code": "import requests\nimport re\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass RatesClient:\n    \"\"\"Client for interacting with the Rates API.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, token: str, base_url: str = \"https://api.rates.example.com/v1\") -> None:\n        self._token = token\n        self.base_url = base_url\n        self.session = requests.Session()\n        self.session.headers.update({\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {self._token}\"})\n\n    def latest(self, currency: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Fetch latest rates for a given currency code.\"\"\"\n        if not re.match(r\"^[A-Z]{3}$\", currency):\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid currency format. Expected 3-letter uppercase code.\")\n\n        try:\n            response = self.session.get(f\"{self.base_url}/latest/{currency}\", timeout=5)\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            data = response.json()\n            if \"rates\" not in data:\n                raise ValueError(\"Unexpected response schema\")\n            return data[\"rates\"]\n        except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n            # Log error appropriately in production\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"API request failed: {e}\")"
}
